1
00:00:00,646 --> 00:00:03,066
- Oh, boy, I was afraid of this.
- What?

2
00:00:03,232 --> 00:00:05,732
(Howard:)These instructions
are a pictographic representation...

3
00:00:05,901 --> 00:00:08,741
(Howard:)...of the least imaginative way
to assemble these components.

4
00:00:08,904 --> 00:00:11,744
(Howard:)This right here
is why Sweden has no space program.

5
00:00:13,075 --> 00:00:16,165
(Penny:)- It looked pretty good in the store.
- It is an inefficient design.

6
00:00:16,328 --> 00:00:17,908
(Leonard:)For example,
Penny has a flatscreen TV...

7
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:20,120
...which means all this space
behind it is wasted.

8
00:00:20,291 --> 00:00:22,921
- We could put her stereo back there.
- And control it how?

9
00:00:23,085 --> 00:00:27,385
(Sheldon:)Run an infrared repeater,
photocell here, emitter here, easy-peasy.

10
00:00:28,048 --> 00:00:30,468
- Good point. How will you cool it?
- Guys, I got this.

11
00:00:30,634 --> 00:00:32,804
- Hang on, Penny.
- How about fans?

12
00:00:32,970 --> 00:00:36,390
(Sheldon:)- Here and here.
- Also inefficient, and might be loud.

13
00:00:36,557 --> 00:00:39,097
How about a liquid cooler?
A little aquarium pump here.

14
00:00:39,268 --> 00:00:40,768
Run some quarter-inch PVC...

15
00:00:40,936 --> 00:00:42,766
(Penny:)Guys, this is actually really simple.

16
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,110
(Howard:)Hold on, honey, men at work.

17
00:00:47,484 --> 00:00:50,944
PVC comes here. Maybe a little
corrugated sheet metal as a radiator here.

18
00:00:51,113 --> 00:00:54,573
(Leonard:)Show me where we put a drip tray,
a sluice and a overflow reservoir?

19
00:00:54,742 --> 00:00:57,662
If water's involved,
we'll ground the crap out of the thing.

20
00:00:57,828 --> 00:01:01,498
(Penny:)Guys, it's hot in here.
I think I'll just take off all my clothes.

21
00:01:06,295 --> 00:01:07,965
(Leonard:)Oh, I've got it.

22
00:01:08,964 --> 00:01:13,714
What if we replaced panels A, B and F and
crossbar H with aircraft-grade aluminum?

23
00:01:13,886 --> 00:01:16,056
(Sheldon:)- Entire thing's one big heat sink.
- Perfect.

24
00:01:16,222 --> 00:01:19,812
Leonard and Sheldon, go to the junkyard
and pick up 6 square meters of aluminum.

25
00:01:19,975 --> 00:01:22,765
- Raj and I will get the oxyacetylene torch.
- Meet in an hour?

26
00:01:22,937 --> 00:01:24,687
(Leonard:)- Done.
- Got it.

27
00:01:27,566 --> 00:01:29,856
(Penny:)Okay, this place does look pretty good.

